],"issn_org":["0008543X"],"issue":"6","journal":"Cancer","pages":"913-926","status":"p","title":"Cancer","volume":"130"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85178394580"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-1beebf15-cc63-4586-99e3-d358aac310ff"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Identification of genetically predicted DNA methylation markers associated with non–small cell lung cancer risk among 34,964 cases and 448,579 controls","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-809205","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"This critique presents and discusses the research contributing to and following the creation and exhibition of the interactive Extended Reality (XR) installation called UDREDNING (English: Diagnosing), which aims to convey the experience of being a parent to a child undergoing socio-medical diagnosis for a rare disease. Being a parent in such a situation often entails great affective and emotional uncertainty, heavy logistics and numerous encounters with people and (digital) systems within social welfare services, public healthcare and bureaucracies. Since these children are pre-diagnosis, they rarely fit neatly into the existing systems, which they must engage with. Due to the open-ended nature of such processes, parents often find themselves alone and marginalized, in lack of an overview, and unsure where to get the help they need. Based on diaries, social media entries and interviews with parents to children during or recently after their experiences of a diagnosing process, an artist created UDREDNING in collaboration with the two authors. The installation uses digital sound, video and a tablet that extends the reality of these parents so people can relate to their experiences of the uncertainties and systemic entanglements characterizing their situation. In this article, we explore the different forms of critique opened by the research and exhibition of the project through concepts across STS, HCI, design and art. We argue that UDREDNING creates an embodied and experiential space of critical resonance extending lived experience into a digital re-activation in an affectively engaging interactive setup.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Gad, Christopher","Fritsch, Jonas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-776459"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Extended reality","Human Computer Interaction","Parental experiences","Science and Technology Studies"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"udredning an extended reality artwork for affectively engaging with diagnosing processes","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85206575123","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-776459","identifier":[{"id":"85206575123","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-f4a4b58a-122e-4db0-8731-62f4e040626b"],"keyword":["Extended Reality","Human-Computer Interaction","Interactive art installation","Parental experiences","Science and Technology Studies"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0D6AC73DBD7441F6D554653A8CFFC4B5"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Information Security and Trust","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christopher","key":"gadpau","last":"Gad","locid":"d55dab65-fffe-4da4-a383-cfcf5ee3a8cd","name":"Gad, Christopher","orcid":"0000-0002-1631-5483","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas","key":"fritschpau","last":"Fritsch","locid":"d37cba38-dff2-4c27-a515-226cfadfd849","name":"Fritsch, Jonas","orcid":"0000-0001-9065-2843","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3677045.3685491","pages":"1-9","status":"p","subtitle":"Adjunct Proceedings of the 2024 Nordic Conference on Human-Computer Interaction","title":"NordiCHI '24"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85206575123"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-f4a4b58a-122e-4db0-8731-62f4e040626b"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"UDREDNING: : an Extended Reality Artwork for Affectively Engaging with Diagnosing Processes","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-776459","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"This chapter explores effects of the implementation of artificial intelligence (AI) on the organisation of work in the Danish Customs and Tax Administration in a situation where a machine learning algorithm was expected to make the work of customs officers more efficient. The chapter highlights how experiments with machine learning algorithms may redraw intra-organisational boundaries, responsibilities, as well as divisions and meanings of work. The implementation of the machine learning algorithm, as a particular form of AI, in this case, led attention towards data and IT systems, at the expense of the very work the technology was intended to support. One concern at play here, we argue, is that AI developers seem to have generally abandoned the idea of representing work, making it ever more important that ethnographers do so.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Jørgensen, Bastian","Gad, Christopher","Winthereik, Brit Ross"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381363"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Artificial intelligence","Ethnography","Machine learning","Organisational Boundaries","Work efficiency"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"organising artificial intelligence and representing work","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.taylorfrancis.com/chapters/edit/10.4324/9781003084471-7/organising-artificial-intelligence-representing-work-bastian-j%C3%B8rgensen-christopher-gad-brit-ross-winthereik","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381363","ids":["itu-06b4c152-8e1d-4b09-ba43-282bdc60a14e"],"keyword":["Artificial Intelligence","Ethnography","Machine Learning","Organisational Boundaries","Work Efficiency"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-D44858FFF940705A6F5A3A4923B9F7B4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.taylorfrancis.com/chapters/edit/10.4324/9781003084471-7/organising-artificial-intelligence-representing-work-bastian-j%C3%B8rgensen-christopher-gad-brit-ross-winthereik","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bastian","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","name":"Jørgensen, Bastian","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christopher","key":"gadpau","last":"Gad","locid":"d55dab65-fffe-4da4-a383-cfcf5ee3a8cd","name":"Gad, Christopher","orcid":"0000-0002-1631-5483","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Brit Ross","key":"winthereikpau","last":"Winthereik","name":"Winthereik, Brit Ross","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Débora","key":"lanzenipedh","last":"Lanzeni","name":"Lanzeni, Débora","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Karen","key":"waltorppedh","last":"Waltorp","name":"Waltorp, Karen","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Sarah","key":"pinkpedh","last":"Pink","name":"Pink, Sarah","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Rachel C.","key":"smithpedh","last":"Smith","name":"Smith, Rachel C.","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9781003084471"],"isbn":["9781350144910"],"publisher":"Bloomsbury Publishing","status":"p","title":