{"abstract":"What does art have to lend to Science and Technology Studies (STS)? Might we see art and its display in museums and galleries as a method of performing STS ‘by material means’? And what roles might STS scholars play in art-science collaborations? Drawing on our experiences with collaborations at the intersections of contemporary art and biology, we explore the similarities and overlapping practices of these knowledge communities and make a series of observations about the potential of the area of Art, Science, and Technology Studies (ASTS) to refigure and complicate the art-science landscape. Our analysis emphasizes the museum as a material public forum and curation as a form of knowing, histories of art and science, and examples of scholarly facilitation and intervention in art-science. We examine emerging patterns in ASTS scholarship and emerging roles for STS scholars as facilitators, participant-observers, curators, and collaborators, particularly in art-science institutions and newly emerging STS and art contexts in Denmark, and specifically, the Medical Museion. Our analysis reveals the persistent third leg of curation, cultural history, or STS as party to collaborations between artists and scientists.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Rogers, Hannah Star","Hussey, Kristin D.","Whiteley, Louise","Bencard, Adam","Gad, Christopher","Abrantes, Eduardo"],"cuid":["S03-096.05-822876"],"event":{"end":"2022-06-03","place":"Århus, dk","start":"2022-06-02","title":"Danish Association for Science and Technology Studies Conference 2022","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2023-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"keyword":["Art","Bioart biology and art","Biology","Categories","Curation as knowledge making","Science","Science and Technology Studies","Technology Studies","bioart","social construction of knowledge","social construction of knowledge categories"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"curating complexities in art science and medicine art science and technology studies asts in public practice","src":["itu","ku","ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.7146/stse.v15i2.139814","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-096.05-822876","ids":["itu-6decf5c1-8b2c-45a1-9422-3530fcc9929d","ku-13f7bdf2-22e7-41ef-90a1-65d9759c3726","ruc-cbb7e2ed-33b4-488c-a178-5434849ab5c4"],"keyword":["Art","Bioart, biology and art","Science","Technology Studies","bioart","biology","categories","curation as knowledge-making","science and technology studies","social construction of knowledge","social construction of knowledge categories"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-07361D83862B3CA97C0A41A2E118D7AF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/99931310/15_2_Rogers_et_al_Complexities_2023_2.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/458849277/15_2_Rogers_et_al_Complexities_2023_2.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.7146/stse.v15i2.139814","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://tidsskrift.dk/encounters/article/view/139814/183843","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Eu