Forlag","status":"p","subtitle":"En introduktion til STS","title":"Videnskab, teknologi og samfund"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-6f76f547-f8bc-4662-be4f-39ef2206ef31"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Postkoloniale STS-studier","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-192958","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Background: In international trials, glucagon-like protein-1 receptor agonists (GLP-1RAs) and sodium-glucose cotransporter-2 inhibitors (SGLT2Is) were effective in improving cardiovascular (CV) outcomes. Methods: We assessed the effect of GLP-1RAs and SGLT2Is treatment effect on CV endpoints by geographical region in multiple international trials using random effects weighted least squares meta-regressions. Results: The estimated effects of both SGLT2Is and GLP-1RAs on major adverse CV events (MACE) in North America (SGLT2Is n = 12,399, HR 0.90, 95% CI 0.81-1.01; GLP-1RAs n = 12,515, HR 0.95, 95% CI 0.83- 1.09) and in Europe (SGLT2Is n = 19,435, HR 0.93, 95% CI 0.85-1.02; GLP-1RAs n = 22,812, HR 0.88, 95% CI 0.79-0.99) were numerically lower but not statistically different to the rest of the world (ROW) (SGLT2Is n = 15,127, HR 0.83, 95% CI 0.75-0.92, p-value for interaction 0.26; GLP-1RAs n = 17,494, HR 0.82, 95% CI 0.73-0.92, p-value for interaction 0.28). Effects of SGLT2Is on heart failure readmission or CV death varied significantly by region (P = 0.0094). The effect of SGLT2Is was significantly smaller in Europe (n = 18,653, HR 0.86, 95% CI 0.78-0.95) than in the ROW (n = 12,463, HR 0.68, 95% CI 0.61-0.76, P = 0.0024). The smaller effect in North America (n = 9776, HR 0.76, 95% CI 0.66-0.87) did not differ significantly from that in the ROW (P = 0.2370). Conclusion: The effects of SGLT2Is on HF events are larger in the ROW. Further analyses and studies are needed to better elucidate the differential effects of SGLTIs and GLP-1RAs by geographical regions.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Cotter, Gad","Davison, Beth A.","Edwards, Christopher","Senger, Stefanie","Teerlink, John R.","Zannad, Faiez","Nielsen, Olav Wendelboe","Metra, Marco","Mebazaa, Alexandre","Chioncel, Ovidiu","Greenberg, Barry H.","Maggioni, Aldo P.","Ertl, Georg","Sato, Naoki","Cohen-Solal, Alain"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-393895"],"filters":{"added":"2022-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["France","Germany","Italy","Japan","Romania","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Associazione Nazionale Medici Cardiologi Ospedalieri","Carol Davila University of Medicine and Pharmacy","Institut National de la Santé et de la Recherche Médicale (INSERM)","Momentum Research, Inc","Nippon Medical School","Paris-Cité University","University of Brescia","University of California San Francisco","University of California at Los Angeles","University of Lorraine","University of Würzburg"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"regional variation of effects of new antidiabetic medications in cardiovascular outcome trials","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/332605824/Regional_variation_of_effects_of_new_antidiabetic_medications.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-393895","identifier":[{"id":"34107289","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85110278781","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-00ba93e0-9290-4894-980a-30be00fe364e"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-AE357AB838F34E0B055659DDCC170F03"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/332605824/Regional_variation_of_effects_of_new_antidiabetic_medications.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"momentum research inc","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Momentum Research, Inc","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"fr","key":"insti