{"abstract":"DNase I hypersensitive sites (DHS) are abundant in regulatory elements, such as promoter, enhancer and transcription factor binding sites. Many studies have revealed that disease-associated variants were concentrated in DHS-related regions. However, limited studies are available on the roles of DHS-related variants in lung cancer. In this study, we performed a large-scale case-control study with 20 871 lung cancer cases and 15 971 controls to evaluate the associations between regulatory genetic variants in DHS and lung cancer susceptibility. The expression quantitative trait loci (eQTL) analysis and pathway-enrichment analysis were performed to identify the possible target genes and pathways. In addition, we performed motif-based analysis to explore the lung-cancer-related motifs using sequence kernel association test. Two novel variants, rs186332 in 20q13.3 (C>T, odds ratio [OR] = 1.17, 95% confidence interval [95% CI]: 1.10-1.24, P = 8.45 × 10-7) and rs4839323 in 1p13.2 (T>C, OR = 0.92, 95% CI: 0.89-0.95, P = 1.02 × 10-6) showed significant association with lung cancer risk. The eQTL analysis suggested that these two SNPs might regulate the expression of MRGBP and SLC16A1, respectively. What's more, the expression of both MRGBP and SLC16A1 was aberrantly elevated in lung tumor tissues. The motif-based analysis identified 10 motifs related to the risk of lung cancer (P < 1.71 × 10-4). Our findings suggested that variants in DHS might modify lung cancer susceptibility through regulating the expression of surrounding genes. This study provided us a deeper insight into the roles of DHS-related genetic variants for lung cancer.","author_count":37,"contributors":["Dai, Juncheng","Li, Zhihua","Amos, Christopher I","Hung, Rayjean J","Tardon, Adonina","Andrew, Angeline S","Chen, Chu","Christiani, David C","Albanes, Demetrios","van der Heijden, Erik H F M","Duell, Eric J","Rennert, Gad","Mckay, James D","Yuan, Jian-Min","Field, John K","Manjer, Jonas","Grankvist, Kjell","Le Marchand, Loic","Teare, M Dawn","Schabath, Matthew B","Aldrich, Melinda C.","Tsao, Ming-Sound","Lazarus, Philip","Lam, Stephen","Bojesen, Stig E","Arnold, Susanne","Wu, Xifeng","Haugen, Aage","Janout, Vladimir","Johansson, Mikael","Brhane, Yonathan","Fernandez-Somoano, Ana","Kiemeney, Lambertus A","Davies, Michael P A","Zienolddiny, Shanbeh","Hu, Zhibin","Shen, Hongbing"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-455982"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Asia, Middle East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Canada","China","Czechia","France","Israel","Netherlands","Norway","Spain","Sweden","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","British Columbia Cancer Agency","CIBER - Centro de Investigacion Biomedica en Red","Carmel Medical Center","Dartmouth College","Fred Hutchinson Cancer Research Center","Harvard University","Institute Catala Oncologia","International Agency for Research on Cancer","Lund University","Moffitt Cancer Center","Nanjing Medical University","National Institute of Occupational Health","National Institutes of Health","Palacký University Olomouc","Radboud University Nijmegen","Skåne University Hospital","Umeå University","University Health Network","University of Hawai'i at Mānoa","University of Kentucky","University of Liverpool","University of Oviedo","University of Pittsburgh","University of Sheffield","University of Texas Health Science Center at Houston","University of Toronto","Vanderbilt University","Washington State University Spokane"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"systematic analyses of regulatory variants in dnase i hypersensitive sites identified two novel lung cancer susceptibility loci","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"http://europepmc.org/Copyright","type":"rem","url":"http://europepmc.org/articles/pmc6783905?pdf=render","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-455982","identifier":[{"id":"30590402","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC6783905","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85066163672","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-68bde63f-0486-4859-ad74-6fea9e849d39"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-39C13E43494F35964093904E0C5CB58C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"http://europepmc.org/Copyright","type":"rem","url":"http://europepmc.org/articles/pmc6783905?pdf=render","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"nanjing medical university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Nanjing Medical University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"dartmouth college","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Dartmouth College","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"ca","key":"university of toronto","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Toronto","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"es","key":"university of oviedo","loc":["Spain","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Oviedo","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"es","key":"ciber centro de investigacion biomedica en red","loc":["Spain","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"CIBER - Centro de Investigacion Biomedica en Red","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"us","key":"fred hutchinson cancer research center","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Fred Hutchinson Cancer Research Center","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"us","key":"harvard university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Harvard University","used":1},{"affno":"8","country":"us","key":"national institutes of health","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"