,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Zhibin","key":"hupau","last":"Hu","name":"Hu, Zhibin","rank":36,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Hongbing","key":"shenpau","last":"Shen","name":"Shen, Hongbing","rank":37,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30590402"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/carcin/bgy187","issn":["01433334","14602180"],"issn_org":["01433334"],"issue":"3","journal":"Carcinogenesis","pages":"432-440","status":"p","title":"Carcinogenesis","volume":"40"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85066163672"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-68bde63f-0486-4859-ad74-6fea9e849d39"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Systematic analyses of regulatory variants in DNase I hypersensitive sites identified two novel lung cancer susceptibility loci","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-455982","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Organization is increasingly entwined with databased governance infrastructures. Developing the idea of ‘infrastructure as partial connection’ with inspiration from Marilyn Strathern and Science and Technology Studies, this article proposes that database infrastructures are intrinsic to processes of organizing intra- and inter-organizational relations. Seeing infrastructure as partial connection brings our attention to the ontological experimentation with knowing organizations through work of establishing and cutting relations. We illustrate this claim through a multi-sited ethnographic study of ‘The Data Warehouse’. ‘The Data Warehouse’ is an important infrastructural component in the current reorganization of Danish educational governance which makes schools’ performance public and comparable. We suggest that ‘The Data Warehouse’ materializes different, but overlapping, infrastructural experiments with governing education at different organizational sites enacting a governmental hierarchy. Each site can be seen as belonging to the same governance infrastructure but also as constituting ‘centres’ in its own right. ‘The Data Warehouse’ participates in the always-unfinished business of organizational world making and is made to (partially) relate to different organizational concerns and practices. This argument has implications for how we analyze the organizational effects of pervasive databased governance infrastructures and invites exploring their multiple organizing effects.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Ratner, Helene Friis","Gad, Christopher"],"cuid":["S02-096.30-021877"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Database Governance Infrastructures","Education","Ethnographic study","Ethnography","Grundskole","Information technology","Infrastructure","Ontological Experimentation","Ontology","Organizational Relations","Partial Connection","Science and Technology Studies","Uddannelsespolitik"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"data warehousing organization infrastructural experimentation with educational governance","src":["au","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83490672/For_open_access_repository.docx","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-096.30-021877","identifier":[{"id":"85058715099","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-7e1b3430-8799-4140-9c5a-d4f27698e642","itu-a38a8cff-090e-48dc-b416-b7a1d738e4f2"],"keyword":["Database Governance Infrastructures","Education","Ethnographic Study","Grundskole","Ontological Experimentation","Organizational Relations","Science and Technology Studies","Uddannelsespolitik","ethnography","information technology","infrastructure","ontology","partial connection"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-0EA6BB052E6BD023038F7919F7D2D0B2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83490672/For_open_access_repository.docx","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Humanities (HUM)","Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, Danish School of Education, Danish School of Education - Education Studies, Emdrup"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Helene Gad","key":"ratnerpau","last":"Ratner","locid":"2dc9be03-8ac6-4767-939f-b1f302353a39","name":"Ratner, Helene Friis","name_org":"Ratner, Helene Gad","orcid":"0000-0002-0842-4049","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Christopher","key":"gadpau","last":"Gad","locid":"d55dab65-fffe-4da4-a383-cfcf5ee3a8cd","name":"Gad, Christopher","orcid":"0000-0002-1631-5483","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1177/1350508418808233","issn":["13505084","14617323"],"issn_org":["13505084"],"issue":"4","journal":"Organization","pages":"537-552","publisher":"SAGE Publications Ltd","status":"p","title":"Organization","volume":"26"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85058715099"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-7e1b3430-8799-4140-9c5a-d4f27698e642","itu-a38a8cff-090e-48dc-b416-b7a1d738e4f2"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Data warehousing organization : Infrastructural experimentation with educational governance","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-096.30-021877","year":2019,"yearsub":2019}
{"abstract":"The development of cancer is driven by the accumulation of many oncogenesis-related genetic alterations and tumorigenesis is triggered by complex networks of involved genes rather than independent actions. To explore the epistasis existing among oncogenesis-related genes in lung cancer development, we conducted pairwise genetic interaction analyses among 35,031 SNPs from 2027 oncogenesis-related genes. The genotypes from three independent genome-wide association studies including a total of 24,037 lung cancer patients and 20,401 healthy controls with Caucasian ancestry were analyzed in the study. Using a two-stage study design including discovery and replication studies, and stringent Bonferroni correction for multiple statistical analysis, we identified significant genetic interactions between SNPs in RGL1:RAD51B (OR=0.44, p value=3.27x10-11 in overall lung cancer and OR=0.41, p value=9.71x10-11 in non-small cell lung cancer), SYNE1:RNF43 (OR=0.73, p value=1.01x10-12 in adenocarcinoma) and FHIT:TSPAN8 (OR=1.82, p value=7.62x10-11 in squamous cell carcinoma) in our analysis. None of these genes have been identified from previous main effect association studies in lung cancer. Further eQTL gene expression analysis in lung tissues provided information supporting the functional role of the identified epistasis in lung tumorigenesis. Gene set enrichment analysis revealed potential pathways and gene networks underlying molecular mechanisms in overall lung cancer as well as histology subtypes development. Our results provide evidence that genetic interactions between oncogenesis-related genes play an important role in lung tumorigenesis and epistasis analysis, combined with functional annotation, provides a valuable tool for uncovering functional novel susceptibility genes that contribute to lung cancer development by interacting with other modifier genes.","author_count":80,"contributors":["Li, Yafang","Xiao, Xiangjun","Bossé, Yohan","Gorlova, Olga","Gorlov, Ivan","Han, Younghun","Byun, Jinyoung","Leighl, Natasha","Johansen, Jakob S","Barnett, Matt","Chen, Chu","Goodman, Gary","Cox, Angela","Taylor, Fiona","Woll, Penella","Wichmann, H Erich","Manz, Judith","Muley, Thomas","Risch, Angela","Rosenberger, Albert","Han, Jiali","Siminovitch, Katherine","Arnold, Susanne M","Haura, Eric B","Bolca, Ciprian","Holcatova, Ivana","Janout, Vladimir","Kontic, Milica","Lissowska, Jolanta","Mukeria, Anush","Ognjanovic, Simona","Orlowski, Tadeusz M","Scelo, Ghislaine","Swiatkowska, Beata","Zaridze, David","Bakke, Per","Skaug, Vidar","Zienolddiny, Shanbeh","Duell, Eric J","Butler, Lesley M","Houlston, Richard","Artigas, María Soler","Grankvist, Kjell","Johansson, Mikael","Shepherd, Frances A","Marcus, Michael W","Brunnström, Hans","Manjer, Jonas","Melander, Olle","Muller, David C","Overvad, Kim","Trichopoulou, Antonia","Tumino, Rosario","Liu, Geoffrey","Bojesen, Stig E","Wu, Xifeng","Le Marchand, Loic","Albanes, Demetrios","Bickeböller, Heike","Aldrich, Melinda C","Bush, William S","Tardon, Adonina","Rennert, Gad","Teare, M Dawn","Field, John K","Kiemeney, Lambertus A","Lazarus, Philip","Haugen, Aage","Lam, Stephen","Schabath, Matthew B","Andrew, Angeline S","Bertazzi, Pier Alberto","Pesatori, Angela C","Christiani, David C","Caporaso, Neil","Johansson, Mattias","McKay, James D","Brennan, Paul","Hung, Rayjean J","Amos, Christopher I"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-013581"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Austria","Canada","Czechia","France","Germany","Greece","Italy","Netherlands","Norway","Poland","Serbia","Spain","Sweden","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Baylor College of Medicine","Bellvitge Biomedical Research Institute","British Columbia Cancer Agency","CIBER - Centro de Investigacion Biomedica en Red","Case Western Reserve University","Catalan Institute of Oncology-ICO","Dartmouth College","Department of Clinical Neurobiology/A230, Heidelberg University Hospital at DKFZ, Im Neuenheimer Feld 280, 69120 Heidelberg, Germany. k.khodosevich@dkfz-heidelberg.de","Fred Hutchinson Cancer Center","Fred Hutchinson Cancer Research Center","German Centre for Cardiovascular Research","Harvard University","Heidelberg University ","Helenic Health Foundation","Hellenic Health Foundation","Helmholtz Association of German Research Centres","Imperial College London","Indiana University Bloomington","Institute of Cancer Research","International Agency for Research on Cancer (IARC)","Laval University","Lund University","Maria Sklodowska-Curie Institute of Oncology","Moffitt Cancer Center","National Institute of Occupational Health","National Institutes of Health","National Institutes of Health (NIH)","Nofer Institute of Occupational Medicine","Nofer Institute of Occupational Medicine, Department of Environmental Epidemiology, Lodz, Poland.","Princess Margaret Cancer Centre","Radboud University Nijmegen","Samuel Lunenfeld Research Institute, Mount Sinai Hospital, Toronto","The National Institute for Health Research Collaboration for Leadership in Applied Health Research and Care West (NIHR CLAHRC West) at University Hospitals Bristol NHS Foundation Trust, Bristol, UK.","The University Medical Center Göttingen","Umeå University","Universite Laval","University Health Network","University Hospital Heidelberg","University of Belgrade","University of Bergen","University of California at Berkeley","University of Göttingen","University of Hawai'i at Mānoa","University of Hawaii at Manoa","University of Kentucky","University of Liverpool","University of Milan","University of Ostrava","University of Oviedo","University of Pittsburgh","University of Salzburg","University of Sheffield","University of Texas MD Anderson Cancer Center","University of Toronto","Vanderbilt University","Washington State University Spokane"],"k