I-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-856ac399-aabf-49f0-bde8-19de1ed2fba9"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Datawarehousing Organization","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383232","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Purpose: Radon is a risk factor for lung cancer and uranium miners are more exposed than the general population. A genome-wide interaction analysis was carried out to identify genomic loci, genes or gene sets that modify the susceptibility to lung cancer given occupational exposure to the radioactive gas radon. Methods: Samples from 28 studies provided by the International Lung Cancer Consortium were pooled with samples of former uranium miners collected by the German Federal Office of Radiation Protection. In total, 15,077 cases and 13,522 controls, all of European ancestries, comprising 463 uranium miners were compared. The DNA of all participants was genotyped with the OncoArray. We fitted single-marker and in multi-marker models and performed an exploratory gene-set analysis to detect cumulative enrichment of significance in sets of genes. Results: We discovered a genome-wide significant interaction of the marker rs12440014 within the gene CHRNB4 (OR = 0.26, 95% CI 0.11–0.60, p = 0.0386 corrected for multiple testing). At least suggestive significant interaction of linkage disequilibrium blocks was observed at the chromosomal regions 18q21.23 (p = 1.2 × 10 −6 ), 5q23.2 (p = 2.5 × 10 −6 ), 1q21.3 (p = 3.2 × 10 −6 ), 10p13 (p = 1.3 × 10 −5 ) and 12p12.1 (p = 7.1 × 10 −5 ). Genes belonging to the Gene Ontology term “DNA dealkylation involved in DNA repair” (GO:0006307; p = 0.0139) or the gene family HGNC:476 “microRNAs” (p = 0.0159) were enriched with LD-blockwise significance. Conclusion: The well-established association of the genomic region 15q25 to lung cancer might be influenced by exposure to radon among uranium miners. Furthermore, lung cancer susceptibility is related to the functional capability of DNA damage signaling via ubiquitination processes and repair of radiation-induced double-strand breaks by the single-strand annealing mechanism.","author_count":39,"contributors":["Rosenberger, Albert","Hung, Rayjean J.","Christiani, David C.","Caporaso, Neil E.","Liu, Geoffrey","Bojesen, Stig E","Le Marchand, Loic","Haiman, Ch A.","Albanes, Demetrios","Aldrich, Melinda C.","Tardon, Adonina","Fernández-Tardón, G.","Rennert, Gad","Field, John K.","Kiemeney, B.","Lazarus, Philip","Haugen, Aage","Zienolddiny, Shanbeh","Lam, Stephen","Schabath, Matthew B.","Andrew, Angeline S.","Brunnsstöm, Hans","Goodman, Gary E.","Doherty, Jennifer A.","Chen, Chu","Teare, M. Dawn","Wichmann, H. Erich","Manz, Judith","Risch, Angela","Muley, Thomas R.","Johansson, Mikael","Brennan, Paul","Landi, Maria Teresa","Amos, Christopher I.","Pesch, Beate","Johnen, Georg","Brüning, Thomas","Bickeböller, Heike","Gomolka, Maria"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-468413"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, Middle East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Austria","Canada","France","Germany","Israel","Netherlands","Norway","Spain","Sweden","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","BfS","Clalit Health Services","Dartmouth College","Fred Hutchinson Cancer Research Center","Harvard University","Heidelberg University ","Helmholtz Zentrum München - German Research Center for Environmental Health","International Agency for Research on Cancer","Ludwig Maximilian University of Munich","Lund University","National Institute of Occupational Health","National Institutes of Health","Radboud University Nijmegen","Ruhr University Bochum","Swedish Medical Group","Technical University of Munich","Translational Lung Research Center Heidelberg (TLRC-H)","Umeå University","University of British Columbia","University of Göttingen","University of Hawai'i at Mānoa","University of Liverpool","University of Oviedo","University of Salzburg","University of Sheffield","University of South Florida","University of Southern California","University of Toronto","University of Utah","Vanderbilt University","Washington State University Spokane"],"keyword":["DNA repair","GWAS","Gene Environment Interaction","Occupational Exposure"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"genetic modifiers of radon induced lung cancer risk a genome wide interaction study in former uranium miners","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"http://europepmc.org/Copyright","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC6375683/pdf/nihms-1007564.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-468413","identifier":[{"id":"PMC6375683","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85049594611","type":"scopus"},{"id":"29971594","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-7d32fef3-fe5c-4d64-b7e8-deb2a900f0fd"],"keyword":["DNA repair","GWAS","Gene–environment interaction","Occupational exposure","Radon progeny"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A0FBF994239D9FDA8B2B053D66BB8E6A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"http://europepmc.org/Copyright","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC6375683/pdf/nihms-1007564.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"university of göttingen","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Göttingen","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"ca","key":"university of toronto","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Toronto","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"harvard university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Harvard University","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"national institutes of health","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"National Institutes of Health","used":1},{"affn