ence Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-247543","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"This article investigates how disability can work analytically as a ‘critique from within’. Our case is the accommodation of citizens with disabilities during the voting process in Denmark. Here disability makes explicit how Danish democracy is produced as disability rubs up against implicit, normalized and mundane infrastructures and practices. We investigate disability as critique in this sense of affording a both analytic and practical ‘breakup’. To do so, we promote a ‘compositionist’ post-actor-network theory approach to disability and to polling and investigate what entry-point for critique this offers. We analyze an incident at a polling booth during the 2013 Danish Municipal election. This renders visible some of the complex socio-material processes through which citizens and the Danish state co-enact and co-authorize one another. We highlight how ‘detachments’ are vital to such processes and we examine parts of the historical background for the production of authority in the context of managing disability as exception during polling. In doing so we point out that as the organization of electoral processes evolves, new potentialities for infra-critique also emerge.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Gad, Christopher","Dalsgaard, Steffen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382456"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Compositionism","Detachment","Disability","Elections","Infra critique"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"disability as infra critique a compositionist approach to the election process in denmark","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/81976799/Disability_as_infra_critique_a_compositionist_approach_to_the_election_process_in_Denmark_preprint_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382456","identifier":[{"id":"85019129765","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-4f5511f1-001d-4c84-a292-8062ea821a18"],"keyword":["Disability","compositionism","detachment","elections","infra-critique"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C94D7D73E61D9D0D0517D47D46042D2C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/81976799/Disability_as_infra_critique_a_compositionist_approach_to_the_election_process_in_Denmark_preprint_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice","The Department, TiP and Games Section"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christopher","key":"gadpau","last":"Gad","locid":"d55dab65-fffe-4da4-a383-cfcf5ee3a8cd","name":"Gad, Christopher","orcid":"0000-0002-1631-5483","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Steffen","key":"dalsgaardpau","last":"Dalsgaard","locid":"bc7a60f7-45a0-401f-813f-6b4aa700c849","name":"Dalsgaard, Steffen","orcid":"0000-0003-3712-6988","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/17530350.2017.1312485","issn":["17530350","17530369"],"issn_org":["17530350"],"issue":"3","journal":"Journal of Cultural Economy","pages":"237-250","publisher":"Routledge","status":"p","title":"Journal of Cultural Economy","volume":"10"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85019129765"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-4f5511f1-001d-4c84-a292-8062ea821a18"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Disability as infra-critique : A compositionist approach to the election process in Denmark","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382456","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"This article discusses how a small place – the polling booth – can be bounded as an ethnographic site with reference to the political and democratic event that it is supposed to facilitate. Concerns about the socio-material bounding of the booth form the main empirical case – a debate, which recently occurred in Denmark when the government proposed to digitalise voting. Digitalisation here became a controversy because of the potential illicit influences that computer experts argued would enter the polling booth and challenge the secrecy and the privacy of the vote, the transparency of the electoral process, and thus the electoral enactment of democracy itself. In this way the polling booth potentially works as an ethnographic entry point for following shifts in contemporary debates","author_count":2,"contributors":["Dalsgaard, Steffen","Gad, Christopher"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384053"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Democracy","Digitalisation","Elections","Ethnography","Event","Place"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"digital unbounding of the polling booth ethnography in small places","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82086505/Dalsgaard_Gad_2017_Digital_polling_booth.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384053","identifier":[{"id":"85021924924","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-be163cd2-c2c6-495e-98b8-ba5398418323"],"keyword":["democracy","digitalisation","elections","ethnography","event","place"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5910500867ACEBBDCE938F78A06ED11E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82086505/Dalsgaard_Gad_2017_Digital_polling_booth.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Steffen","key":"dalsgaardpau","last":"Dalsgaard","locid":"bc7a60f7-45a0-401f-813f-6b4aa700c849","name":"Dalsgaard, Steffen","orcid":"0000-0003-3712-6988","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christopher","key":"gadpau","last":"Gad","locid":"d55dab65-fffe-4da4-a383-cfcf5ee3a8cd","name":"Gad, Christopher","orcid":"0000-0002-1631-5483","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/00141844.2017.1348379","issn":["00141844","1469588X"],"issn_org":["00141844"],"journal":"Ethnos","pages":"1-16","publisher":"Routledge","status":"p","title":"Ethnos"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85021924924"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-be163cd2-c2c6-495e-98b8-ba5398418323"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Digital Unbounding of the Polling Booth: Ethnography in Small Places","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384053","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Although several lung cancer susceptibility loci have been identified, much of the heritability for lung cancer remains unexplained. Here 14,803 cases and 12,262 controls of European descent were genotyped on the OncoArray and combined with existing data for an aggregated genomewide association study (GWAS) analysis of lung cancer in 29,266 cases and 56,450 controls. We identified 18 susceptibility loci achieving genome-wide significance, including 10 new loci. The new loci highlight the striking heterogeneity in genetic susceptibility across the histological subtypes of lung cancer, with four loci associated with lung cancer overall and six loci associated with lung adenocarcinoma. Gene expression quantitative trait locus (eQTL) analysis in 1,425 normal lung tissue samples highlights RNASET2, SECISBP2L and NRG1 as candidate genes. Other loci include genes such as a cholinergic nicotinic receptor, CHRNA2, and the telomere-related genes OFBC1 and RTEL1. Further exploration of the target genes will continue to provide new insights into the etiology of lung cancer.","author_count":62,"contributors":["McKay, James D.","Hung, Rayjean J.","Han, Younghun","Zong, Xuchen","Carreras-Torres, Robert","Christiani, David C.","Caporaso, Neil E.","Johansson, Mattias","Xiao, Xiangjun","Li, Yafang","Byun, Jinyoung","Dunning, Alison","Pooley, Karen A.","Qian, David C.","Ji, Xuemei","Liu, Geoffrey","Timofeeva, Maria N.","Bojesen, Stig E","Wu, Xifeng","Marchand, Loic Le","Albanes, Demetrios","Bickeböller, Heike","Aldrich, Melinda C.","Bush, William S.","Tardon, Adonina","Rennert, Gad","Teare, M. Dawn","Field, John K.","Kiemeney, Lambertus A.","Lazarus, Philip","Haugen, Aage","Lam, Stephen","Schabath, Matthew B.","Andrew, Angeline S.","Shen, Hongbing","Hong, Yun Chul","Yuan, Jian Min","Bertazzi, Pier Alberto","Pesatori, Angela C.","Ye, Yuanqing","Diao, Nancy","Su, Li","Zhang, Ruyang","Brhane, Yonathan","Leighl, Natasha","Johansen, Jakob S.","Mellemgaard, Anders","Saliba, Walid","Haiman, Christopher A.","Wilkens, Lynne R.","Rafnar, Thorunn","Thorgeirsson, Thorgeir E","Reginsson, Gunnar W.","Brennan, Paul","Landi, Maria Teresa","Amos, Christopher I"],"cuid":["S02-096.67-021743"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Asia, Middle East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corpau":["SpiroMeta Consortium"],"country":["Canada","China","France","Germany","Israel","Italy","Netherlands","Norway","South Korea","Spain","Sweden","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Carlos III Health Institute (ISCIII) (CIBER)","Case Western Reserve University","Dartmouth College","Harvard University","International Agency for Research on Cancer","Moffitt Cancer Center","Nanjing Medical University","National Institute of Occupational Health","National Institutes of Health","National Institutes of Health (NIH)","Radboud University Nijmegen","Samuel Lunenfeld Research Institute, Mount Sinai Hospital, Toronto","Seoul National University","Technion-Israel Institute of Technology","Umeå University","University of British Columbia","University of Cambridge","University of Göttingen","University of Hawai'i at Mānoa","University of Hawaii at Manoa","University of Liverpool","University of Milan","University of Oviedo","University of Pittsburgh","University of Sheffield","University of South Florida","University of Southern California","University of Texas MD Anderson Cancer Center","University of Toronto","Vanderbilt University","Washington State University Pullman","Washington State University Spokane"],"keyword":["Architecture","Consortium","Crohns disease","Genome wide association","Imputation","Metaanalysis","Telomere length","Variants"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-