{"abstract":"In this paper, we compare critical practices on the Danish fishery inspection ship The West Coast to such practices at the Nordic Folk Center for Renewable Energy. These cases are the ingredients for examining the role of critique in organizational experimentation and research. Taking our point of departure in a notion of critique as finding the right proximity introduced by Bruno Latour and Donna Haraway, we discuss alternatives to critique as based on a position detached from the object of critique. Our analysis shows that critique is immanent to the practices we study and already to some extent conceptualized by the practitioners. To further problematize the already ongoing critical engagements in the organizations we study, we relate our ethnographic descriptions to work done on infra critique (Verran, Willerslev). In conclusion, the relation between the notion of critique as infra-critic and scholarly critical practices is commented on. We find proximation to be a useful concept as an infra critical description of ongoing experimentation with professional identities and organizational boundaries.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Gad, Christopher","Winthereik, Brit Ross"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384433"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Ethnography","Etnografi","Infra critique","Infrakritik","Science and Technology Studies STS","Sustainable energy","Vedvarende energi","fisheries inspection","fiskerikontrol","videnskabs og teknologistudier STS"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"infrakritik og proximering om at finde den rette afstand","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/81550688/25059_58268_1_SM.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384433","ids":["itu-d720a33f-1058-466f-9d91-e75696253c77"],"keyword":["Infra critique","Infrakritik","ethnography","etnografi","fisheries inspection","fiskerikontrol","science and technology studies (STS)","sustainable energy","vedvarende energi","videnskabs- og teknologistudier (STS)"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-C92603B198FD854FDF6D6498B01FA811"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/81550688/25059_58268_1_SM.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice","The Department, Interdisciplinary Section"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christopher","key":"gadpau","last":"Gad","locid":"d55dab65-fffe-4da4-a383-cfcf5ee3a8cd","name":"Gad, Christopher","orcid":"0000-0002-1631-5483","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Brit Ross","key":"winthereikpau","last":"Winthereik","name":"Winthereik, Brit Ross","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["09056998","22462589"],"issn_org":["09056998"],"issue":"122","journal":"K & K","pages":"341","publisher":"Forlaget Medusa","status":"p","title":"K & K","volume":"44"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-d720a33f-1058-466f-9d91-e75696253c77"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Infrakritik og proximering : Om at finde den rette afstand","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384433","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Common variants in 94 loci have been associated with breast cancer including 15 loci with genome-wide significant associations (P<5 × 10(-8)) with oestrogen receptor (ER)-negative breast cancer and BRCA1-associated breast cancer risk. In this study, to identify new ER-negative susceptibility loci, we performed a meta-analysis of 11 genome-wide association studies (GWAS) consisting of 4,939 ER-negative cases and 14,352 controls, combined with 7,333 ER-negative cases and 42,468 controls and 15,252 BRCA1 mutation carriers genotyped on the iCOGS array. We identify four previously unidentified loci including two loci at 13q22 near KLF5, a 2p23.2 locus near WDR43 and a 2q33 locus near PPIL3 that display genome-wide significant associations with ER-negative breast cancer. In addition, 19 known breast cancer risk loci have genome-wide significant associations and 40 had moderate associations (P<0.05) with ER-negative disease. Using functional and eQTL studies we implicate TRMT61B and WDR43 at 2p23.2 and PPIL3 at 2q33 in ER-negative breast cancer aetiology. All ER-negative loci combined account for ∼11% of familial relative risk for ER-negative disease and may contribute to improved ER-negative and BRCA1 breast cancer risk prediction.","author_count":273,"contributors":["Couch, Fergus J","Kuchenbaecker, Karoline B","Michailidou, Kyriaki","Mendoza-Fandino, Gustavo A","Nord, Silje","Lilyquist, Janna","Olswold, Curtis","Hallberg, Emily","Agata, Simona","Ahsan, Habibul","Aittomäki, Kristiina","Ambrosone, Christine","Andrulis, Irene L","Anton-Culver, Hoda","Arndt, Volker","Arun, Banu K","Arver, Brita","Barile, Monica","Barkardottir, Rosa B","Barrowdale, Daniel","Beckmann, Lars","Beckmann, Matthias W","Benitez, Javier","Blank, Stephanie V","Blomqvist, Carl","Bogdanova, Natalia V","Bojesen, Stig E","Bolla, Manjeet K","Bonanni, Bernardo","Brauch, Hiltrud","Brenner, Hermann","Burwinkel, Barbara","Buys, Saundra S","Caldes, Trinidad","Caligo, Maria A","Canzian, Federico","