orresponding":null,"first":"Alvaro N A","key":"monteiroalvaronapau","last":"Monteiro","name":"Monteiro, Alvaro N A","rank":246,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Montserrat","key":"garcíaclosasmontserratpau","last":"García-Closas","name":"García-Closas, Montserrat","rank":247,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"43","corresponding":null,"first":"Montserrat","key":"garciaclosasmontserratpau","last":"Garcia-Closas","name":"Garcia-Closas, Montserrat","rank":247,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Douglas F","key":"eastondouglasfpau","last":"Easton","name":"Easton, Douglas F","rank":248,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Antonis C","key":"antoniouantoniscpau","last":"Antoniou","name":"Antoniou, Antonis C","rank":249,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27117709"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/ncomms11375","issn":["20411723"],"journal":"Nature Communications","paperid":"11375","publisher":"Nature Research","status":"p","title":"Nature Communications","volume":"7"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84968760294"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-6b042e05-f70f-4878-ab37-29ba550bfea4","ku-4b8195d6-8bcc-4895-ab16-6f850ff2281b","sdu-75f73ee4-f2c8-4d30-8287-466d077d2b78"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Identification of four novel susceptibility loci for oestrogen receptor negative breast cancer","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-099.71-020467","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"The concept of well-being has become a key category of social and political imagination, cultivating new understandings of 'what it means to be a capable person' (Corsín Jiménez, 2008, 2). In 2015, the Danish Ministry of Education began conducting national, annual measurements of Danish pupils' well-being. This measurement recasts the traditionally qualitative psycho-pedagogical concept of well-being in numerical terms. Moreover, different actors with overlapping but competing calculative techniques enters the scene. We investigate well-being as an emerging object of governance in Denmark with attention to competing techniques for measuring and calculating well-being: 1) the statistical factor and reliability calculations used by the Danish Ministry of Education, used to turn a 40 questions-questionnaire into a 'quality indicator', which again is used to hold institutions accountable to new national objectives for pupils' well-being; 2) the Danish newspaper A4's interactive, online mapping of pupils' well-being at all Danish schools, developed from the same numbers (accessed through their juridical right to access government files) but using different calculative techniques and aimed at communicating to a general public; 3) the 'Københavnerbarometer', an older well-being metrics developed by the municipality of Copenhagen for local governance of schools. We highlight how these different metrics contribute to factualise 'well-being' as evidence of the state of affairs in the public school all the while they also enact different versions of well-being, publics, and the problem-solution nexus.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Ratner, Helene Friis","Gad, Christopher"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-240207"],"event":{"end":"2016-09-03","place":"Barcelona, es","start":"2016-08-31","title":"4S/EASST Conference Barcelona","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"managing danish pupils well being an emerging numerical expertise and its contestations","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-240207","ids":["au-c2539fad-02de-4555-8ca3-04d240025696"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-3218BF7D4F65628351FEEAAA91F78A5A"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, Danish School of Education, Danish School of Education - Education Studies, Emdrup"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Helene Gad","key":"ratnerpau","last":"Ratner","locid":"2dc9be03-8ac6-4767-939f-b1f302353a39","name":"Ratner, Helene Friis","name_org":"Ratner, Helene Gad","orcid":"0000-0002-0842-4049","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Christopher","key":"gadpau","last":"Gad","name":"Gad, Christopher","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-c2539fad-02de-4555-8ca3-04d240025696"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Managing Danish pupils’ well-being : an emerging numerical expertise and its contestations","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-240207","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"author_count":1,"contributors":["Gad, Christopher"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383711"],"event":{"end":"2016-06-03","place":"Aarhus, dk","start":"2016-06-02","title":"Danish STS Conference 2016","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"nostagia in fisheries inspection and critique as infra critique","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-383711","ids":["itu-a7b700f4-9168-4e53-9d63-db82b4121e65"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-5D438C8FAE231D118CD54DE489B35FF5"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice","The Department, TiP and Games Section"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christopher","key":"gadpau","last":"Gad","locid":"d55dab65-fffe-4da4-a383-cfcf5ee3a8cd","name":"Gad, Christopher","orcid":"0000-0002-1631-5483","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-a7b700f4-9168-4e53-9d63-db82b4121e65"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Nostagia in Fisheries Inspection and Critique as infra-critique","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383711","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"This essay discusses the complex relation between the knowledges and practices of the researcher and his/her informants in terms of lateral concepts. The starting point is that it is not the prerogative of the (STS) scholar to conceptualize the world; all our “informants” do it too. This creates the possibility of enriching our own conceptual repertoires by letting them be inflected by the concepts of those we study. In a broad sense, the lateral means that there is a many-to-many relation between domains of knowledge and practice. However, each specific case of the lateral is necessarily immanent to a particular empirical setting and form of inquiry. In this sense lateral concepts are radically empirical since it locates concepts within the field. To clarify the meaning and stakes of lateral concepts, we first make a contrast between lateral anthropology and Latour’s notion of infra-reflexivity. We end with a brief illustration and discussion of how lateral conceptualization can re-orient STS modes of inquiry, and why this matters.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Gad, Christopher","Bruun Jensen, casper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383892"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","OECD"],"country":["Japan"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Osaka Medical and Pharmaceutical University"],"keyword":["Inter reflexivity","infra reflexivity","lateral anthropology","lateral concepts"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"lateral concepts","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.17351/ests2016.77","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383892","ids":["itu-b48158c6-491