l":"Science, Technology & Human Values","publisher":"Sage Publishing","status":"p","title":"Science, Technology & Human Values","volume":"39"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-c638f3a7-168d-4840-8d2e-1042530cc627"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Conceptual And The Empirical : Expanding STS","type":"Editorial","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384176","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Practice has become a topic of increasing empirical and conceptual concern within sociology and neighbouring fields. ‘Practice’ can refer to a location or it can refer to action. It is possible to be ‘in practice’, to ‘have a practice’ or to be ‘constituted by practice’. Practice can be a cause, an effect or an explanation. Within science and technology studies (STS), the practice orientation is simultaneously analytical – in the form of various practice theories – and empirical, in that research objects are often defined as ‘practices’. Focusing on a range of examples, especially ethnomethodological, this paper examines some implications and problems that follow when practice slides unnoticed between empirical and conceptual registers. Arguing that a reconsideration of practice thinking is important in order to retain its vigour, we outline a view of practice as a ‘factish’, at once conceptual and empirical, which facilitates analyses of practical ontologies and their transformations. This informs a final discussion of the politics and promises of practice.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Gad, Christopher","Jensen, Casper Bruun"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381669"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Conceptual empirical interplay","Ethnomethodology","Practical ontologies","Practice theories","Science and Technology Studies STS"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the promises of practice","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/1467-954X.12200","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381669","identifier":[{"id":"84911443300","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-1b2950c7-abfe-4ef6-8ff1-129d44aabff9"],"keyword":["Conceptual-empirical interplay","Ethnomethodology","Practical ontologies","Practice theories","Science and technology studies (STS)"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-8B6A784FBA0418412ADC577A783AFA72"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/1467-954X.12200","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice","The Department, Culture, Aesthetics, Organisations and Society"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christopher","key":"gadpau","last":"Gad","locid":"d55dab65-fffe-4da4-a383-cfcf5ee3a8cd","name":"Gad, Christopher","orcid":"0000-0002-1631-5483","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Casper Bruun","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Casper Bruun","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/1467-954x.12200","issn":["00380261","1467954X"],"issn_org":["00380261"],"issue":"4","journal":"The Sociological Review","publisher":"Sage Publishing","status":"p","title":"The Sociological Review","title_org":"Sociological Review","volume":"62"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-1b2950c7-abfe-4ef6-8ff1-129d44aabff9"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Promises of Practice","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.fors