sh Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-d6476e5e-f49b-4eab-a829-9f2fa9140b11"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A Postplural Attitude : Reflections on subjectivity and ontology","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384419","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"In a combined analysis, we investigate how the movie Minority Report can inform and nuance the vision of technological capacities that we identify in event detection literature. The vision in MR of an effective, pre-emptive and preventive technopolitics reflects important areas of event detection research, but it is also a vision for which the movie has become a common cultural reference. While they express similar conceptions of surveillance and technological potentials, MR also becomes a resource for discussing the broader 'techno'-culture of event detection, showing how surveillance systems are imbued with cultural assumptions and preferences, most notably that technology has strong enabling capacities. By juxtaposing MR and event detection research, we thus demonstrate that it is an important analytical task to understand the assumptions on which such systems are constructed, as well as their social and political implications.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Gad, Christopher","Hansen, Lone Koefoed"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-012955"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Event detection","Minority Report","surveillance systems","techno politics","technological capacities"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a closed circuit technological vision on minority report event detection and enabling technologies","src":["au","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84881267550","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-012955","identifier":[{"id":"84881267550","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-04d761fd-b6fb-405d-968c-01613e4d92eb","itu-d39ea43e