{"abstract":"This article addresses the concept of “industrial interests” and examines its role in a topical controversy about a large research grant from a private foundation, the Novo Nordisk Foundation, to the University of Copenhagen. The authors suggest that the debate took the form of a “public trial” where the grant and close(r) intermingling between industry and public research was prosecuted and defended. First, the authors address how the grant was framed in the media. Second, they redescribe the case by introducing new “evidence” that, because of this framing, did not reach “the court.” The article ends with a discussion of some implications of the analysis, including that policy making, academic research, and public debates might benefit from more detailed accounts of interests and stakes.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Vedel, Jane Bjørn","Gad, Christopher"],"cuid":["S02-091.41-032140"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Research collaboration"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci","soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a public trial de novo rethinking industrial interests","src":["cbs","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S02-091.41-032140","ids":["cbs-dfc9d0b0-142a-463e-bd44-8ec44675e649","itu-9d750abe-ae7b-481e-a238-4785fd2583e2"],"keyword":["industrial interest","metabolic research","research collaboration","science-industry relations"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-73DAB641ABCF6195E752326B0006BAB1"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Organization"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice","The Department, Culture, Aesthetics, Organisations and Society"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jane Bjørn","key":"vedelpau","last":"Vedel","locid":"236a8ec5-6114-4013-a71f-de2bdc87f610","name":"Vedel, Jane Bjørn","orcid":"0000-0002-1894-8401","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Christopher","key":"gadpau","last":"Gad","locid":"d55dab65-fffe-4da4-a383-cfcf5ee3a8cd","name":"Gad, Christopher","orcid":"0000-0002-1631-5483","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1177/0270467611422839","issn":["02704676","15524183"],"issn_org":["02704676"],"issue":"6","journal":"Bulletin of Science, Technology & Society","pages":"506-517","publisher":"SAGE Publications Inc.","status":"p","title":"Bulletin of Science, Technology & Society","volume":"31"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-dfc9d0b0-142a-463e-bd44-8ec44675e649","itu-9d750abe-ae7b-481e-a238-4785fd2583e2"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School","ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A Public Trial De Novo : Rethinking “Industrial Interests”","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-091.41-032140","year":2012,"yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"As a concept, culture can easily appear quite diffuse and it is often contested. This ambiguity begs the question of what it means to invoke the concept in particular situations. This paper is an analytic experiment, which was kick-started when I asked informants about sailor culture during fieldwork onboard the Danish fisheries inspection vessel The West Coast. In response, fisheries inspectors, surprisingly, suggested watching the Danish cult movie Martha (1967). I describe this incident as a small ethnographic moment leading me to conduct the present experiment. This involves using Martha as an analytic device to investigate sailor culture. More specifically, I use a preliminary analysis of the movie as an entry point to understand five matters of concern, which I encountered during fieldwork. With point of departure in an analytic attitude I call empirical philosophy I propose the term inter-reflexivity to characterize this mode of lateral cultural analysis. Inter-reflexivity emphasizes a double movement emerging from an ethnographic moment in the field and the creative translation of that moment into an analytic device. The paper concludes by discussing the implications of using a popular cultural artefact encountered in the field as such a device for articulating some complex, current stakes in fisheries inspection and ‘inventing’ a particular version of sailor culture.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Gad, Christopher"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384277"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Empirical philosophy","Freedom","Inter reflexivity","Nostalgia","Technology","ethnographic moment","fisheries inspection","lateral analysis","post actor network theory","sailor culture"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"what we talk about when we talk about sailor culture understanding danish fisheries inspection through a cult movie","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-384277","ids":["itu-cda91770-4ecc-11df-b794-000ea68e967b"],"keyword":["Inter-reflexivity","empirical philosophy","ethnographic moment","fisheries inspection","freedom","lateral analysis","nostalgia","post-actor-network theory","sailor culture","technology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-B5718273B1AE1D142707C46A75B3E442"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christopher","key":"gadpau","last":"Gad","locid":"d55dab65-fffe-4da4-a383-cfcf5ee3a8cd","name":"Gad, Christopher","orcid":"0000-0002-1631-5483","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["20001525"],"journal":"Culture Unbound: Journal of Current Cultural Research","pages":"367-392","publisher":"Linköping University Press","status":"p","title":"Culture Unbound: Journal of Current Cultural Research","volume":"4"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-cda91770-4ecc-11df-b794-000ea68e967b"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"What we talk about when we talk about sailor culture : Understanding Danish Fisheries Inspection through a Cult Movie","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384277","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
